{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_2F8P5LGjh9xuyedFTpAvbgyP","content":"1\tdiff --git a/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md b/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md\n2\tindex 5789a746..e7f029a9 100644\n3\t--- a/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md\n4\t+++ b/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md\n5\t@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@ accepted-negative claim, or equality projection is introduced for these rows.\n6\t \n7\t An independent audit re-derives the credited arities and fixture paths from\n8\t the two raw C traces. Kondo reports zero errors and warnings. The full oracle\n9\t-runs 26 tests and 1,689 assertions with exactly one failure and no errors:\n10\t+runs 26 tests and 1,695 assertions with exactly one failure and no errors:\n11\t its retained `(= :pass (:gate-status evidence))` closure assertion. The\n12\t unexercised arities — **58** under the current accounting, including\n13\t `parse/1` — therefore continue to block acceptance. Verification results are\n14\tdiff --git a/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj b/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\n15\tindex afcbe899..53da3a0f 100644\n16\t--- a/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\n17\t+++ b/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\n18\t@@ -1930,9 +1930,28 @@\n19\t (def ^:private kernel-declarations\n20\t   \"The declared dispositions: explicit, versioned input to classification.\n21\t    Generated evidence is never their source of truth; provenance is in-file.\n22\t-   A declaration whose revalidation guards fail leaves its row a blocker,\n23\t+   The file's contract is validated at load: version and provenance are\n24\t+   fixed, and every historical disposition must retain its exact boundary\n25\t+   and a complete record - the file is authoritative for this metadata, and\n26\t+   a load-time failure means the file was edited beyond its contract. A\n27\t+   declaration whose revalidation guards fail leaves its row a blocker,\n28\t    not a deviation.\"\n29\t-  (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn\"))))\n30\t+  (let [parsed (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn\")))\n31\t+        complete? (fn [d required] (every? d required))\n32\t+        portability-required [:call :script :message :boundary :upstream-value :reason]\n33\t+        upstream-required [:call :boundary :reason :upstream-revision]]\n34\t+    (assert (and (= 1 (:version parsed)) (= \"ea18c8e4^\" (:provenance parsed)))\n35\t+            \"the declarations file's version/provenance are part of its contract\")\n36\t+    (doseq [[id d] (:portability parsed)]\n37\t+      (assert (and (complete? d portability-required)\n38\t+                   (= :nonportable-host-value (:boundary d)))\n39\t+              (str \"incomplete or out-of-scope portability declaration: \" id)))\n40\t+    (doseq [[id d] (:upstream-failures parsed)]\n41\t+      (assert (and (complete? d upstream-required)\n42\t+                   (contains? #{:upstream-unbound-definition :upstream-malformed-proof-sequence}\n43\t+                              (:boundary d)))\n44\t+              (str \"incomplete or out-of-scope upstream-failure declaration: \" id)))\n45\t+    parsed))\n46\t \n47\t (defn- kernel-callable-descriptor?\n48\t   \"True when `value` is the shape of the admitted common-call descriptor the\n49\t@@ -2112,6 +2131,15 @@\n50\t       (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n51\t                                              (assoc-in (c-with descriptor) [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data :script] '())\n52\t                                              (c-with descriptor))))\n53\t+      ;; Shape-only mutation: identical contents delivered as a list in A\n54\t+      ;; while C keeps the vector - the raw shape comparison refuses it even\n55\t+      ;; though the vec-normalized declaration guard alone would not.\n56\t+      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture\n57\t+                                             (assoc-in a [:outcome :thrown :data :script]\n58\t+                                                       (apply list script))\n59\t+                                             a\n60\t+                                             (c-with descriptor)\n61\t+                                             (c-with descriptor))))\n62\t       ;; Descriptor forgeries refuse.\n63\t       (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n64\t                                              (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/admission))\n65\t@@ -2134,6 +2162,18 @@\n66\t                                              (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/outcomes?))))\n67\t           \"a descriptor with a missing outcomes marker fails\")\n68\t       (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with {:type :closure}) (c-with {:type :closure}))))\n69\t+      ;; A descriptor copied across calls: the structurally valid\n70\t+      ;; check-after-qed descriptor submitted under the elab-after-qed\n71\t+      ;; fixture refuses through the declared-call pin - the copy carries\n72\t+      ;; another call's identity. (Two descriptors of the SAME call with\n73\t+      ;; identical payloads are the same deviation claim; their witness\n74\t+      ;; authenticity is the compiler's admission check.)\n75\t+      (is (nil? (let [other (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability :check-after-qed])\n76\t+                      other-descriptor (assoc descriptor :yang.call/entry (values/closure nil {})\n77\t+                                              :clj/admission (values/closure nil {}))]\n78\t+                  (kernel-host-value-deviation (assoc fixture :call (:call other))\n79\t+                                               a a (c-with other-descriptor) (c-with other-descriptor))))\n80\t+          \"a descriptor copied across calls fails the declared-call pin\")\n81\t       ;; A mutated declaration (declared message != live failure) fails the guard.\n82\t       (with-redefs [kernel-declarations (assoc-in kernel-declarations\n83\t                                                   [:portability :elab-after-qed :message]"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_HdbryOetZWHNYkFIkHPttCxU","content":"1925\t       :missing-dependency (when (and (empty? direct) (empty? integration))\n1926\t                             (get kernel-unexercised-reasons [symbol n]\n1927\t                                  \"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\"))})))\n1928\t\n1929\t\n1930\t(def ^:private kernel-declarations\n1931\t  \"The declared dispositions: explicit, versioned input to classification.\n1932\t   Generated evidence is never their source of truth; provenance is in-file.\n1933\t   The file's contract is validated at load: version and provenance are\n1934\t   fixed, and every historical disposition must retain its exact boundary\n1935\t   and a complete record - the file is authoritative for this metadata, and\n1936\t   a load-time failure means the file was edited beyond its contract. A\n1937\t   declaration whose revalidation guards fail leaves its row a blocker,\n1938\t   not a deviation.\"\n1939\t  (let [parsed (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_declarations.edn\")))\n1940\t        complete? (fn [d required] (every? d required))\n1941\t        portability-required [:call :script :message :boundary :upstream-value :reason]\n1942\t        upstream-required [:call :boundary :reason :upstream-revision]]\n1943\t    (assert (and (= 1 (:version parsed)) (= \"ea18c8e4^\" (:provenance parsed)))\n1944\t            \"the declarations file's version/provenance are part of its contract\")\n1945\t    (doseq [[id d] (:portability parsed)]\n1946\t      (assert (and (complete? d portability-required)\n1947\t                   (= :nonportable-host-value (:boundary d)))\n1948\t              (str \"incomplete or out-of-scope portability declaration: \" id)))\n1949\t    (doseq [[id d] (:upstream-failures parsed)]\n1950\t      (assert (and (complete? d upstream-required)\n1951\t                   (contains? #{:upstream-unbound-definition :upstream-malformed-proof-sequence}\n1952\t                              (:boundary d)))\n1953\t              (str \"incomplete or out-of-scope upstream-failure declaration: \" id)))\n1954\t    parsed))\n1955\t\n1956\t(defn- kernel-callable-descriptor?\n1957\t  \"True when `value` is the shape of the admitted common-call descriptor the\n1958\t   reconciled compiler publishes for a guest closure: a true function-type\n1959\t   marker, an entry that is a minted closure, and an admission witness.\n1960\t   Structurally invalid shapes - a bare `{:type :closure}` map, a scalar or\n1961\t   missing entry, a missing or non-closure witness, an outcomes marker that\n1962\t   is missing or false - fail. Descriptor AUTHENTICITY (that the witness is\n1963\t   this compiler's own mint, not a copy) is the compiler's admission check\n1964\t   upstream of the outcome; this predicate is the test-side structural\n1965\t   half, and the payload/message/call guards around it carry revalidation.\"\n1966\t  [value]\n1967\t  (and (map? value)\n1968\t       (= :function (:clj/type value))\n1969\t       (true? (:clj/outcomes? value))\n1970\t       (values/closure? (get value :yang.call/entry))\n1971\t       (values/closure? (get value :clj/admission))))\n1972\t\n1973\t(defn- kernel-host-value-deviation\n1974\t  [fixture a b walker semantic]\n1975\t  ;; Disposition only: keep every original comparison and all four outcomes.\n1976\t  ;; A new failure outside this exact host-value boundary remains a mismatch.\n1977\t  ;; The declared call, boundary, upstream value and reason come from the\n1978\t  ;; versioned declarations file; the guards revalidate the live execution\n1979\t  ;; against the declaration - the pinned call, the declared message and\n1980\t  ;; script - so a changed execution cannot ride a copied declaration.\n1981\t  (let [id (:id fixture)\n1982\t        declared (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability id])]\n1983\t    (when (and declared\n1984\t               (contains? #{:elab-after-qed :check-after-qed} id)\n1985\t               (= (:call fixture) (:call declared))\n1986\t               (= :completed (:status a) (:status b) (:status walker) (:status semantic))\n1987\t               (= (:outcome a) (:outcome b))\n1988\t               (= (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data :meta])\n1989\t                  {:nonportable-host-value (str (class clojure.core/meta))})\n1990\t               ;; The declaration must describe THIS failure: same message and\n1991\t               ;; same script (top-level sequential shape normalized), or the\n1992\t               ;; guard fails and the row stays a blocker.\n1993\t               (= (:message declared) (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :message]))\n1994\t               (= (vec (:script declared))\n1995\t                  (vec (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data :script])))\n1996\t               (every? (fn [c]\n1997\t                         (and (= :yin.k/error (first (:outcome c)))\n1998\t                              (= (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :message])\n1999\t                                 (get-in c [:outcome 1 :yin.k/message]))\n2000\t                              (= (dissoc (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data]) :meta)\n2001\t                                 (dissoc (get-in c [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data]) :meta))\n2002\t                              (= (result-shape (dissoc (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data]) :meta))\n2003\t                                 (result-shape (dissoc (get-in c [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data]) :meta)))\n2004\t                              (let [meta (get-in c [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data :meta])]\n2005\t                                ;; Both representations the pipeline actually\n2006\t                                ;; produces: a pre-adoption raw closure, or the\n2007\t                                ;; admitted §8.10 descriptor. Anything else -\n2008\t                                ;; including an invented `{:type :closure}` map -\n2009\t                                ;; fails.\n2010\t                                (or (values/closure? meta)\n2011\t                                    (kernel-callable-descriptor? meta)))))\n2012\t                       [walker semantic]))\n2013\t      {:boundary (:boundary declared)\n2014\t       :upstream-value (:upstream-value declared)\n2015\t       :evidence {:file \"slice9_evidence.edn\" :fixture-id id\n2016\t                  :path [:a :outcome :thrown :data :meta]}\n2017\t       :reason (:reason declared)})))\n2018\t\n2019\t\n2020\t(defn- kernel-upstream-failure\n2021\t  \"Disposition for two pinned upstream failures. The declared boundary,\n2022\t   reason and upstream revision come from the versioned declarations file;\n2023\t   the guards pin the original call and every observed boundary. A new\n2024\t   failure must still block the gate.\"\n2025\t  [fixture a b walker semantic]\n2026\t  (let [declared (get-in kernel-declarations [:upstream-failures (:id fixture)])\n2027\t        completed-c? (= :completed (:status walker) (:status semantic))\n2028\t        c (:outcome walker)\n2029\t        same-c? (= c (:outcome semantic))\n2030\t        unbound-message \"Pinned upstream declaration has no definition\"\n2031\t        unbound-data {:refusal :upstream-unbound :binding 'latte-kernel.typing/type-of-ascribe}\n2032\t        failure\n2033\t        (when (and declared completed-c? same-c?)\n2034\t          (case (:id fixture)\n2035\t            :typing-ascription\n2036\t            (when (and (= (:call fixture) (:call declared))\n2037\t                       (= :blocked (:status a))\n2038\t                       (= \"class java.lang.IllegalStateException\" (:exception a))\n2039\t                       (= \"Attempting to call unbound fn: #'latte-kernel.typing/type-of-ascribe\" (:message a))\n2040\t                       (= :completed (:status b))\n2041\t                       (= {:thrown {:message unbound-message :data unbound-data}} (:outcome b))\n2042\t                       (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message unbound-message :yin.k/data unbound-data}] c))\n2043\t              {:boundary (:boundary declared)\n2044\t               :reason (:reason declared)})\n2045\t            :compile-malformed\n2046\t            (when (and (= (:call fixture) (:call declared))\n2047\t                       (= :blocked (:status a) (:status b))\n2048\t                       (= \"class java.lang.IllegalArgumentException\" (:exception a) (:exception b))\n2049\t                       (= \"Don't know how to create ISeq from: java.lang.Long\" (:message a) (:message b))\n2050\t                       (nil? (:data a)) (nil? (:data b))\n2051\t                       (= [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"seq of a non-collection is not supported\"\n2052\t                                         :yin.k/data {:value 42}}] c))\n2053\t              {:boundary (:boundary declared)\n2054\t               :reason (:reason declared)})\n2055\t            nil))]\n2056\t    (when failure\n2057\t      (assoc failure :upstream-revision (:upstream-revision declared)\n2058\t             :evidence {:file \"slice9_evidence.edn\" :fixture-id (:id fixture)\n2059\t                        :paths [[:a] [:b] [:c-walker] [:c-semantic]]}))))\n2060\t\n2061\t\n2062\t(deftest test-kernel-acceptance-counting\n2063\t  (let [inventory [{:symbol 'latte-kernel.syntax/subst :arities [2 3] :disposition :admitted}\n2064\t                   {:symbol 'latte-kernel.syntax/term? :arities [1] :disposition :admitted}]\n2065\t        fixture {:id :direct-subst :call '(latte-kernel.syntax/subst x y)}\n2066\t        calls '[[gate-syntax-subst 2]]\n2067\t        rows [{:id :direct-subst :status :pass\n2068\t               :c-walker {:executed-calls calls} :c-semantic {:executed-calls calls}}\n2069\t              {:id :check-assume-have-discharge :status :pass\n2070\t               :included-functions ['gate-syntax-subst]\n2071\t               :c-walker {:executed-calls calls} :c-semantic {:executed-calls calls}}]\n2072\t        entries (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture] rows)]\n2073\t    (is (= [:direct :unexercised :unexercised] (mapv :exercise entries))\n2074\t        \"An admitted but uncalled arity stays uncredited despite static membership\")\n2075\t    (is (empty? (:integration-fixture-ids (second entries))))\n2076\t    (is (= [:unexercised :unexercised :unexercised]\n2077\t           (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n2078\t                                                    (mapv #(assoc % :status :mismatch) rows)))))\n2079\t    (let [observed (mapv #(-> %\n2080\t                              (assoc-in [:c-walker :executed-calls] '[[gate-syntax-subst 2] [gate-syntax-subst 3]])\n2081\t                              (assoc-in [:c-semantic :executed-calls] '[[gate-syntax-subst 2] [gate-syntax-subst 3]])) rows)]\n2082\t      (is (= [:direct :named-integration :unexercised]\n2083\t             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture] observed))))\n2084\t      (is (= [:direct :named-integration :unexercised]\n2085\t             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n2086\t                                                      (mapv #(dissoc % :included-functions) observed)))))\n2087\t      (is (= [:direct :unexercised :unexercised]\n2088\t             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n2089\t                                                      (assoc-in observed [1 :id] :unnamed-integration))))))\n2090\t    (doseq [lane [:c-walker :c-semantic]]\n2091\t      (is (= [:unexercised :unexercised :unexercised]\n2092\t             (mapv :exercise (kernel-exercise-entries inventory [fixture]\n2093\t                                                      (mapv #(dissoc % lane) rows))))\n2094\t          \"Both C lanes must demonstrate the exact arity\")))\n2095\t  (let [script (vector [:qed '(lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}] [:qed 'missing {}])\n2096\t        declared-call (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability :elab-after-qed :call])\n2097\t        fixture {:id :elab-after-qed :call declared-call}]\n2098\t    (is (= (vec (:script (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability :elab-after-qed]))) (vec script))\n2099\t        \"The controls model the declared script exactly\")\n2100\t    (let [a {:status :completed\n2101\t             :outcome {:thrown {:message \"Wrong proof script: proof steps after qed.\"\n2102\t                                :data {:script script\n2103\t                                       :meta {:nonportable-host-value (str (class clojure.core/meta))}}}}}\n2104\t          descriptor {:yang.call/entry (values/closure nil {})\n2105\t                      :clj/type :function\n2106\t                      :clj/outcomes? true\n2107\t                      :clj/admission (values/closure nil {})}\n2108\t          c-with (fn [meta]\n2109\t                   {:status :completed\n2110\t                    :outcome [:yin.k/error {:yin.k/message \"Wrong proof script: proof steps after qed.\"\n2111\t                                            :yin.k/data {:script script :meta meta}}]})]\n2112\t      ;; Both representations the reconciled pipeline actually produces.\n2113\t      (is (some? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2114\t                                             (c-with (values/closure nil {})) (c-with (values/closure nil {})))))\n2115\t      (is (some? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor)))\n2116\t          \"The admitted §8.10 descriptor classifies as the declared deviation\")\n2117\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation (assoc fixture :id :other) a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n2118\t      ;; The declared-call pin: a mutated call refuses.\n2119\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation (assoc fixture :call '(latte-kernel.proof/elab-proof env [] (quote [[:qed :wrong]])))\n2120\t                                             a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor)))\n2121\t          \"a mutated call fails the declared-call pin\")\n2122\t      ;; Per-lane incompleteness: each of the four executions must be complete.\n2123\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture (assoc a :status :blocked) a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n2124\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a (assoc a :status :blocked) (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n2125\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (assoc (c-with descriptor) :status :blocked) (c-with descriptor))))\n2126\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with descriptor) (assoc (c-with descriptor) :status :blocked))))\n2127\t      ;; Payload and shape mutations refuse.\n2128\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2129\t                                             (assoc-in (c-with descriptor) [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data :script] [:new-mismatch])\n2130\t                                             (c-with descriptor))))\n2131\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2132\t                                             (assoc-in (c-with descriptor) [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data :script] '())\n2133\t                                             (c-with descriptor))))\n2134\t      ;; Shape-only mutation: identical contents delivered as a list in A\n2135\t      ;; while C keeps the vector - the raw shape comparison refuses it even\n2136\t      ;; though the vec-normalized declaration guard alone would not.\n2137\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture\n2138\t                                             (assoc-in a [:outcome :thrown :data :script]\n2139\t                                                       (apply list script))\n2140\t                                             a\n2141\t                                             (c-with descriptor)\n2142\t                                             (c-with descriptor))))\n2143\t      ;; Descriptor forgeries refuse.\n2144\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2145\t                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/admission))\n2146\t                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/admission))))\n2147\t          \"a descriptor without its admission witness fails\")\n2148\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2149\t                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :yang.call/entry :not-a-closure))\n2150\t                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :yang.call/entry :not-a-closure))))\n2151\t          \"a descriptor whose entry is not a minted closure fails\")\n2152\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2153\t                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/type :data))\n2154\t                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/type :data))))\n2155\t          \"a descriptor with a wrong type marker fails\")\n2156\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2157\t                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/outcomes? false))\n2158\t                                             (c-with (assoc descriptor :clj/outcomes? false))))\n2159\t          \"a descriptor with a false outcomes marker fails\")\n2160\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a\n2161\t                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/outcomes?))\n2162\t                                             (c-with (dissoc descriptor :clj/outcomes?))))\n2163\t          \"a descriptor with a missing outcomes marker fails\")\n2164\t      (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with {:type :closure}) (c-with {:type :closure}))))\n2165\t      ;; A descriptor copied across calls: the structurally valid\n2166\t      ;; check-after-qed descriptor submitted under the elab-after-qed\n2167\t      ;; fixture refuses through the declared-call pin - the copy carries\n2168\t      ;; another call's identity. (Two descriptors of the SAME call with\n2169\t      ;; identical payloads are the same deviation claim; their witness\n2170\t      ;; authenticity is the compiler's admission check.)\n2171\t      (is (nil? (let [other (get-in kernel-declarations [:portability :check-after-qed])\n2172\t                      other-descriptor (assoc descriptor :yang.call/entry (values/closure nil {})\n2173\t                                              :clj/admission (values/closure nil {}))]\n2174\t                  (kernel-host-value-deviation (assoc fixture :call (:call other))\n2175\t                                               a a (c-with other-descriptor) (c-with other-descriptor))))\n2176\t          \"a descriptor copied across calls fails the declared-call pin\")\n2177\t      ;; A mutated declaration (declared message != live failure) fails the guard.\n2178\t      (with-redefs [kernel-declarations (assoc-in kernel-declarations\n2179\t                                                  [:portability :elab-after-qed :message]\n2180\t                                                  \"A different declared failure\")]\n2181\t        (is (nil? (kernel-host-value-deviation fixture a a (c-with descriptor) (c-with descriptor))))\n2182\t        \"carrying a declaration forward means revalidating it, not copying it\"))))\n2183\t\n2184\t"}
